[1m[38;5;231mWhat makes a task one you "care about"?[0m

[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;153mImplicit involvement (Recommended)[39m
     [38;5;246mYou're notified about tasks you're assigned to, created, or commented on. Zero UI, zero stored subscription state —
[39m     [38;5;246mit's derivable from the task itself. Cheap to add explicit following later; hard to take away once people rely on [39m
     [38;5;246mit.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m Implicit + explicit follow
     [38;5;246mInvolvement subscribes you automatically, plus a follow/unfollow button for anything else. Needs a subscriptions [39m
     [38;5;246mtable and mute semantics (what happens when you unfollow a task you're assigned to?). More power, more edge cases.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m Per-list or per-project
     [38;5;246mYou subscribe to a whole list and hear about everything in it. Presumes tasks are grouped, which sub-project one [39m
     [38;5;246mhasn't decided yet — this choice would constrain that design.[39m
  [38;5;246m4.[39m Mentions only
     [38;5;246mYou hear only when someone names you directly. Very low noise, but misses the "my assigned task was closed" case [39m
     [38;5;246mthat started this conversation.[39m
